{
  "id": "29079_iiharu",
  "headword": "{言|い}い{張|は}る",
  "reading": "いいはる",
  "romaji": "iiharu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to insist (stubbornly); to assert firmly; to maintain",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to insist (stubbornly); to assert firmly; to maintain (one's claim)",
      "explanation": "To stubbornly hold to and keep asserting one's own opinion or claim, refusing to back down even when challenged. Often carries a nuance of unreasonable stubbornness."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29079_iiharu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{自分|じぶん}は{悪|わる}くないと{言|い}い{張|は}る。",
      "english": "He insists he did nothing wrong.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29079_iiharu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼女|かのじょ}は{何|なに}も{知|し}らないと{言|い}い{張|は}った。",
      "english": "She insisted that she knew nothing.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29079_iiharu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{証拠|しょうこ}を{見|み}せても、{彼|かれ}は{自分|じぶん}が{正|ただ}しいと{言|い}い{張|は}って{譲|ゆず}らなかった。",
      "english": "Even when shown the evidence, he kept insisting he was right and would not give in.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "To keep firmly asserting one's claim and refuse to yield, often with a connotation of obstinacy. Typically takes a quoted statement marked with と.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- 〜と{言|い}い{張|は}る: to insist that ～\n- {最後|さいご}まで{言|い}い{張|は}る: to keep insisting to the end\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {主張|しゅちょう}する: to assert — neutral; states one's position without the stubborn nuance\n- {言|い}い{張|は}る: stresses refusing to back down",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
